hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1552.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from his father that in a letter which the Messenger of Allah"
"1552.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from his father that in a letter which the Messenger of Allah"
"1553.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab estimated the full blood-money for the people of urban areas. For those who had gold"
"1553.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab estimated the full blood-money for the people of urban areas. For those who had gold"
"1554.1",""
"1554.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said"
"1555.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Marwan ibn al-Hakam wrote to Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan that a madman was brought to him who had killed a man. Muawiya wrote to him"
"1555.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Marwan ibn al-Hakam wrote to Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan that a madman was brought to him who had killed a man. Muawiya wrote to him"
"1556.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Irak ibn Malik and Sulayman ibn Yasar that a man of the Banu Sad ibn Layth was running a horse and it trod on the finger of a man from the Juhayna tribe. It bled profusely"
"1556.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Irak ibn Malik and Sulayman ibn Yasar that a man of the Banu Sad ibn Layth was running a horse and it trod on the finger of a man from the Juhayna tribe. It bled profusely"
"1557.1","Mālik related to me, from Hishām ibn ‘Urwah, from his father, that a *mukhannath* (a man effeminate in appearance and manner) was with Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may Allāh bless him and grant him peace. He said to ‘Abdullāh ibn Abī Umayyah, while the Messenger of Allāh, may Allāh bless him and grant him peace, was listening: \"O ‘Abdullāh, if Allāh grants you victory over Ṭā’if tomorrow, I will guide you to the daughter of Ghaylān, for she turns with four (hips) and turns away with eight.\" The Messenger of Allāh, may Allāh bless him and grant him peace, said: \"These people should not enter upon you.\""
"1557.2","Mālik related to me, from Abī al-Zinād, that he said: ‘Umar ibn ‘Abd al-‘Azīz flogged a slave eighty lashes for slander. Abī al-Zinād said: I asked ‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Āmir ibn Rabī‘ah about that, and he said: I lived during the time of ‘Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, ‘Uthmān ibn ‘Affān, and the Caliphs thereafter, and I did not see anyone flog a slave for slander more than forty lashes."
"1558.1","Malik related to me that the generally agreed on way of doing things amongst the community about an accident is that there is no blood-money until the victim is better. If a man's bone"
"1558.2","Malik related to me that the generally agreed on way of doing things amongst the community about an accident is that there is no blood-money until the victim is better. If a man's bone"
"1559.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab and also Urwa ibn az-Zubayr said the same as Said ibn al-Musayyab said about a woman. Her blood-money from a man is the same up to a third of the blood-money of a man. If what she is owed exceeds a third of the blood-money of the man"
"1559.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab and also Urwa ibn az-Zubayr said the same as Said ibn al-Musayyab said about a woman. Her blood-money from a man is the same up to a third of the blood-money of a man. If what she is owed exceeds a third of the blood-money of the man"
"1560.1",""
"1560.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Ibn Shihab say"
"1561.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf from Abu Hurayra that a woman from the Hudhayl tribe threw a stone at a woman from the same tribe"
"1561.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf from Abu Hurayra that a woman from the Hudhayl tribe threw a stone at a woman from the same tribe"
"1562.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah"
"1562.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah"
"1563.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman said"
"1563.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman said"
"1564.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said ibn al- Musayyab used to say"
"1564.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said ibn al- Musayyab used to say"
"1565.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that he asked Ibn Shihab about the one-eyed man who gouged out the eye of a healthy person. Ibn Shihab said"
"1565.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he asked Ibn Shihab about the one-eyed man who gouged out the eye of a healthy person. Ibn Shihab said"
"1566.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Zayd ibn Thabit used to say"
"1566.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Zayd ibn Thabit used to say"
"1567.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Sulayman ibn Yasar mention that a face wound in which the bone was bared was like a head wound in which the bone was bared"
"1567.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Sulayman ibn Yasar mention that a face wound in which the bone was bared was like a head wound in which the bone was bared"
"1568.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said"
"1568.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said"
"1569.1",""
"1569.2","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Yahya ibn Said, that it reached him that Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, Salim ibn Abdullah, and Urwah ibn Az-Zubayr used to say: If a runaway slave steals something for which the prescribed punishment is amputation, he is to be amputated."
"1570.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr allowed retaliation for a head wound which splintered the bone"
"1570.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman that Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr allowed retaliation for a head wound which splintered the bone"
"1571.1","Yahya related to me from Malik, that it reached him that a slave girl was brought to Umar ibn Al-Khattab, whose master had burned her with fire or injured her with it, and he freed her. Malik said: The established practice among us is that the emancipation of a man who has debts that encompass his wealth is not valid, and the emancipation of a boy is not valid until he reaches puberty or the age of puberty. And the emancipation of one under guardianship of his wealth is not valid, even if he reaches puberty, until he manages his own wealth."
"1571.2","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman, that Az-Zubayr ibn Al-Awwam met a man who had apprehended a thief and intended to take him to the ruler. Az-Zubayr interceded for him to let him go. The man said: No, until I take him to the ruler. Az-Zubayr said: When you take him to the ruler, may Allah curse the interceder and the one for whom intercession is made."
"1572.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Muslim ibn Jundub from Aslam"
"1572.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Muslim ibn Jundub from Aslam"
"1573.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say"
"1573.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say"
"1574.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"1574.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"1575.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn that Abu Ghatafan ibn Tarif al-Murri informed him that Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent him to Abdullah ibn Abbas to ask him what there was for the molar. Abdullah ibn Abbas said"
"1575.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn that Abu Ghatafan ibn Tarif al-Murri informed him that Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent him to Abdullah ibn Abbas to ask him what there was for the molar. Abdullah ibn Abbas said"
"1576.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father made all the teeth the same in the blood-money and did not prefer any kind over others. Malik said"
"1576.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father made all the teeth the same in the blood-money and did not prefer any kind over others. Malik said"
"1577.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar said"
"1577.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar said"
"1578.1","Malik related to me that he had heard that Marwan ibn al-Hakam gave a decision about a slave who was injured that the person who injured him had to pay what he had diminished of the value of the slave. Malik said"
"1578.2","Malik related to me that he had heard that Marwan ibn al-Hakam gave a decision about a slave who was injured that the person who injured him had to pay what he had diminished of the value of the slave. Malik said"
"1579.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz gave a decision that when a jew or christian was killed"
"1579.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz gave a decision that when a jew or christian was killed"
"1580.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Sulayman ibn Yasar said"
"1580.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Sulayman ibn Yasar said"
"1581.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"1581.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said"
"1582.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said"
"1582.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said"
"1583","[1583] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Thiqah, on the authority of Bukair ibn Abdullah ibn Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman ibn Al-Hubab Al-Ansari, on the authority of Abu Qatada Al-Ansari: The Messenger of God, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade drinking dates and raisins together. And the beautiful and the fresh are all together. Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 1583 Arabic Hadith:"
"1584.1","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of wala' and its gift."
"1584.2","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Nafi', from Abdullah ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people during one of his military expeditions. Abdullah ibn Umar said: I approached him, but he departed before I reached him. I asked what he had said. It was said to me: He forbade that anything be steeped in gourds and in tarred vessels."
"1585.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Umar ibn al- Khattab demanded of the people at Mina"
"1585.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Umar ibn al- Khattab demanded of the people at Mina"
"1586.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Amr ibn Shuayb that a man of the Banu Mudlij called Qatada threw a sword at his son and it struck his thigh. The wound bled profusely and he died. Suraqa ibn Jusham came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and mentioned that to him Umar said to him"
"1586.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Amr ibn Shuayb that a man of the Banu Mudlij called Qatada threw a sword at his son and it struck his thigh. The wound bled profusely and he died. Suraqa ibn Jusham came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and mentioned that to him Umar said to him"
"1587.1",""
"1587.2","Malik said that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar were asked"
"1588.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that a man of the Ansar called Uhayha ibn al-Julah had a young paternal uncle who was younger than him and who was living with his maternal uncles. Uhayha took him and killed him. His maternal uncles said"
"1588.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr that a man of the Ansar called Uhayha ibn al-Julah had a young paternal uncle who was younger than him and who was living with his maternal uncles. Uhayha took him and killed him. His maternal uncles said"
"1589.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab and Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1589.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Said ibn al- Musayyab and Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah"
"1590.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab killed five or seven people for one man whom they had killed secretly by trickery. Umar said"
"1590.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab killed five or seven people for one man whom they had killed secretly by trickery. Umar said"
"1591.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurara that he had heard that Hafsa"
"1591.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurara that he had heard that Hafsa"
"1592.1","Yahya related to me from Malik from Umar ibn Husayn"
"1592.2","Yahya related to me from Malik from Umar ibn Husayn"
"1593.1","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Marwan ibn al-Hakam wrote to Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan to mention to him that a drunkard was brought to him who had killed a man. Muawiya wrote to him to kill him in retaliation for the dead man. Yahya said that Malik said"
"1593.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Marwan ibn al-Hakam wrote to Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan to mention to him that a drunkard was brought to him who had killed a man. Muawiya wrote to him to kill him in retaliation for the dead man. Yahya said that Malik said"
"1594.1",""
"1594.2","Yahya related to me from Malik that he saw whomever he was satisfied with among the people of knowledge say about a man who willed that his murderer be pardoned when he murdered him intentionally"
"1595.1","Yahya narrated to me, from Malik, from Qatan ibn Wahb ibn Umayr ibn al-Ajda'."
"1595.2",""
